ty/traceability.go, task-board.config.json, untracked UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md and internal/rpcwire/. Root inspected tracked changes: RPC staged docs/ownership hash and one RPC fuzz gate. These are not credentials work.\n7|\n8|A verified byte-for-byte backup exists at the CONTROL ROOT /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910 with manifest.json (15 files, SHA256, original head, tracked/untracked classification), tracked.patch and files/. Re-verify every source/backup byte and current status before changing any listed path. If new or different foreign changes exist, preserve them in an additional verified snapshot first. Attach a task-scoped preservation archive/outcome to the RPC task and record restoration instructions before separation. Preserve original file modes and all evidence; no secrets should be printed.\n9|\n10|To free the candidate scope, you may park ONLY this enumerated RPC delta: after durable verified backup, restore each of the four individually named tracked paths to its checkpoint blob and move the enumerated untracked RPC files into task-scoped preservation storage outside the worktree. Verify every moved byte remains recoverable and retain the backup. No repo-wide reset/restore/checkout/clean, no deletion of original work without verified preservation, no absorption of the RPC delta into this CR. Do not remove other files or .temp evidence. The RPC task remains pending and its old v0.5.0 unresolved note is historical; current v0.6.0 credential requirements settle the direction.\n11|\n12|Then use the documented managed workspace/base refresh flow to incorporate current main and v0.6.0 while preserving checkpointed signed commits and board authority. Do not hand-edit .task-board or hand-synthesize commits, do not reset an accepted checkpoint or change its identity behind the manager. If tooling refuses a safe base transition, report the exact refusal and handle promptly to root