{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aba9-d1ff-7602-bf9f-32a3aa09bb6c"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0"},"call_id":"call_01a0abaa3984703385722c95b54c3e51","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-4-1\",\n  \"command\": \"/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board --help 2>&1 | head -n 80\\necho \\\"===Q HELP===\\\"\\n/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board q --help 2>&1 | head -n 60\",\n  \"description\": \"Check task-board CLI help\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"Manage a file-based task board with epics, stories, tasks, and bugs.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board [command]\\n\\nAvailable Commands:\\n  admin                  Server administration (users, tokens, access)\\n  boards                 List boards accessible to the current user (remote mode)\\n  claude                 Launch Claude through the Task-board Session Manager\\n  codex                  Attach Codex to the Task-board Session Manager\\n  completion             Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\\n  export                 Export current board into a tar.gz archive\\n  goal                   Read and align the board-scoped parent primary goal\\n  grep                   Full-text search across board files\\n  handoff                Verify role handoff evidence and move to the role end status\\n  help                   Help about any command\\n  import                 Import a tar.gz archive into the current board\\n  init                   Install task-board project integrations\\n  limits                 Inspect and control provider rate-limit state\\n  login                  Store a token for the current remote\\n  logout                 Remove active user's token for current remote\\n  m                      Execute a mutation (write operation)\\n  migrate-keychain       Import legacy remote credentials into macOS Keychain\\n  migrate-project-config Preview or apply guarded deprecated project-config alias migration\\n  plan                   Show execution plan with phases and critical path\\n  q                      Query the board with a mini DSL\\n  repair-links           List or remove unsupported container dependency links\\n  resource               Upload, update, download, and delete board resources\\n  self-update            Update task-board to the latest version\\n  session                Inspect and stop Task-board Session Manager sessions\\n  spawn                  Queue an agent spawn run for a board task\\n  switch-user            Switch active user for current remote\\n  tree                   Show board as hierarchical tree\\n  tui                    Launch interactive TUI\\n  validate               Validate board structure\\n  whoami                 Show current remote and active user\\n  worktree               Inspect and repair managed Story workspaces\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n  -h, --help                     help for task-board\\n      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)\\n      --json                     Output in JSON format\\n      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check\\n      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)\\n      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)\\n  -v, --version                  version for task-board\\n\\nUse \\\"task-board [command] --help\\\" for more information about a command.\\n===Q HELP===\\nExecute queries against the board using a compact DSL.\\n\\nOperations:\\n  get(ID)              Get a single element by ID\\n  activity(ID, ...)    Read bounded, cursor-paginated element activity\\n  list(filters...)     List elements with filters\\n  count(filters...)    Count elements matching filters\\n  summary()            Board overview (counts + active/blocked)\\n  plan(scope?)         Execution phases; scope=[ID,ID,...] plans the union of subtrees\\n  agents(stale=N?)     Agent dashboard\\n  models(agent?)       Available models for spawn\\n  project_config()     Full active project board runtime config (always local)\\n  project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=PROVIDER?)\\n                       Narrow effective child-spawn policy for one target\\n  provider_limits()    Machine-scoped provider rate-limit state (always local)\\n  provider_limits(identity=KEY|all_identities=true)\\n                       Report one indexed provider identity, or every one\\n  whoami()             Current remote URL and active user (always local)\\n  schema()             Introspect the full operations/fields/presets contract,\\n                       including the statement grammar (arguments, quoting,\\n                       projection, batching) under \\\"grammar\\\"\\n  schema(operation=NAME|mutation=NAME)\\n                       Return only one typed operation or mutation signature\\n                       plus a one-line \\\"syntax\\\" statement of the grammar\\n\\nField projection:\\n  { id status assignee }     Select specific fields\\n  { overview }               Use a base preset (minimal, default, overview, full, progress, planning)\\n  { observability-task }     Use project observability presets (project, epic, story, task)\\n  (omitted)                  Defaults to { id name status }\\n\\nBatching:\\n  Separate multiple queries with semicolons; results preserve source order\\n\\nSpawn policy projection:\\n  Full project_config reports the effective spawn-policy-v2/v3 contract,\\n  authority, normalized provider and role-effective policy, and exact config\\n  provenance. V2 additionally reports its frozen compatibility snapshot and a\\n  copy-ready v3 migration object; this is read-only evidence and never edits\\n  task-board.config.json. Spawn-preflight returns only the selected role policy\\n  and its actionable migration warning.\\n\\nOutput format:\\n  --format json       Standard JSON (default)\\n  --format compact    Compact tabular output (~40% fewer tokens)\\n                      plan() switches to the super-compact planning shape:\\n                      flat waves of IDs, one-line critical path, id->status map\\n\\nExamples:\\n  task-board q 'schema()'\\n  task-board q 'get(TASK-260211-abc) { id status assignee }'\\n  task-board q 'activity(TASK-260211-abc, limit=25, order=descending, view=effective)'\\n  task-board q 'list(type=task, status=development) { overview }'\\n  task-board q 'count(type=task, status=done)'\\n  task-board q 'summary()'\\n  task-board q 'summary() { observability-project }'\\n  task-board q 'get(STORY-1) { observability-story }'\\n  task-board q 'models()'\\n  task-board q 'models(agent=claude)'\\n  task-board q 'project_config()'\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6171,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1543,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
