{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c545","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aba9-d1ff-7602-bf9f-32a3aa09bb6c"},"sequence":253,"recorded_at":1780531400000501,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0"},"call_id":"call_01a0abaa649573a794b952a3b5935d5e","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md`.\n1|# Write-path census — config-plus-trust pair (TASK-260909-2ez769 rev6)\n2|\n3|Producer: Muse (muse-spark), 2026-09-16. Managed base\n4|`a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903`. This census closes the\n5|CR3/CR4/CR5 crash/coherence family at the class level: every production\n6|code path that creates, replaces, removes or renames `config.toml`, its\n7|backups, `trust.json`, the pending joint-commit marker, the lock file or\n8|the credential files is enumerated with the lock state it requires, the\n9|intent revalidation it performs, its positive test, its interleaving\n10|negative, and its narrowing plant.\n11|\n12|Enforcement: `internal/config/writepath_census_test.go`\n13|(`TestWritePathCensusGate`) statically fails when a pair mutation\n14|appears outside these rows; `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller` is\n15|the control plant proving the gate sees a new unlocked caller. The gate\n16|runs in the normal `go test ./...` suite.\n17|\n18|Conventions: \"exclusive\" is the host-channel authorization lock\n19|(`fileLock.exclusive`), held across the whole listed sequence; \"shared\n20|fast path\" is `lockForConvergedRead` (shared hold, valid only when no\n21|marker is present, since staging a marker needs exclusive).\n22|\n23|## Rows\n24|\n25|### 1. Apply replacement — `replaceDurably` via `JointCommit`\n26|\n27|- Production call site: `applyV4` (`internal/config/migration_v4_apply.go`)\n28|  passes the replace closure to `store.JointCommit`; the closure calls\n29|  `replaceDurably(filesystem, filename, backup, preview.SourceDocument,\n30|  preview.Replacement)`.\n31|- Required lock state: exclusive, held by `JointCommit` across leftover\n32|  convergence, in-lock revalidation, marker staging, replace, bump and\n33|  marker removal.\n34|- Intent revalidation before writing: `revalidateApplyV4` inside the\n35|  hold (current source bytes, source version, rendered preview bytes,\n36|  generation, credential custody) plus the marker backstop\n37|  (`marker.SourceGeneration == committed.Generation`) and the closed\n38|  marker check.\n39|- Positive test: `TestApplyV4HappyPath` (exact installed bytes, backup,\n40|  generation+1).\n41|- Interleaving negative: `TestLoadCoherentSerializesWithJointCommit`\n42|  (coherent reader waits out a held joint commit);\n43|  `TestRevalidateApplyV4StaleSource/StaleGeneration/PreviewMismatch`\n44|  (concurrent change between fast-fail checks and the hold refuses).\n45|- Narrowing plant: `preview-length` (same-length tampered preview\n46|  admitted at the in-lock site; killed by\n47|  `TestRevalidateApplyV4PreviewMismatch`), `apply-gen-direction`\n48|  (newer generation admitted; killed by\n49|  `TestRevalidateApplyV4StaleGeneration`).\n50|\n51|### 2. Rollback replacement — `replaceDurably` via `JointCommit`\n52|\n53|- Production call site: `rollbackV4` passes the replace closure to\n54|  `store.JointCommit`; the closure calls `replaceDurably(filesystem,\n55|  filename, preRollback, snapshot.Document(), backupBytes)`.\n56|- Required lock state: exclusive, same hold as row 1.\n57|- Intent revalidation: `revalidateRollbackV4` inside the hold (current\n58|  document still the pinned source and still differs from the backup,\n59|  backup still decodes below v4, generation pinned); an already-holding\n60|  target returns `errRollbackConverged` before any marker is staged.\n61|- Positive test: `TestRollbackV4` (restored bytes, generation+1,\n62|  second rollback is a no-op).\n63|- Interleaving negative: rollback stale-source/generation revalidation\n64|  tests; the row-1 serialization shape covers the shared hold.\n65|- Narrowing plant: shared with row 1 at the helper level\n66|  (`replaceDurably` is only reachable through these two closures plus\n67|  row 10); rollback-closure-specific:\n68|  `compensate-rollback-source-swap` pins the restore closure (row 3).\n69|\n70|### 3. In-hold compensation restore — `writeTempReplace` via `JointCommit`\n71|\n72|- Production call site: `applyV4`/`rollbackV4` pass the restore closure\n73|  (`writeTempReplace(filesystem, filename, source)`) to\n74|  `store.JointCommit`; `compensateLocked`\n75|  (`internal/hosttrust/joint.go`) runs it after a failed bump without\n76|  releasing the hold. This is the CR5 F1 repair: the previous\n77|  `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` ran unlocked after `JointCommit`\n78|  returned and is deleted.\n79|- Required lock state: exclusive, same continuous hold as the replace\n80|  and the failed bump. No surviving reader, writer or held boundary can\n81|  converge the replacement between the failure and the restore.\n82|- Intent revalidation before writing: the marker is re-read\n83|  (custody-verified, closed decode) and compared pin-for-pin with the\n84|  staged intent; the configuration hash must equal the replacement pin\n85|  (source-present skips the restore; anything else refuses with the\n86|  marker kept); after the restore the bytes are re-read and must equal\n87|  the source pin before the marker aborts. Committed trust is\n88|  deliberately never re-read: the fault that broke the bump must not\n89|  break the abort, and an apparently durable bump is unproven exactly\n90|  because its commit reported failure.\n91|- Positive tests: `TestJointCommitCompensatesBumpFailure` (hosttrust),\n92|  `TestApplyV4CompensatesBumpFailure` /\n93|  `TestRollbackV4CompensatesBumpFailure` (production entries; clean\n94|  abort, original bump refusal preserved).\n95|- Interleaving negatives (deterministic, gated-restore rendezvous):\n96|  `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` (ported CR5\n97|  probe; reader blocks, then observes the aborted pair),\n98|  `TestRollbackV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit`,\n99|  `TestApplyV4CompensationSerializesWithWriter` /\n100|  `TestRollbackV4CompensationSerializesWithWriter` (revocation commits\n101|  after the abort),\n102|  `TestApplyV4CompensationSerializesWithBoundary` /\n103|  `TestRollbackV4CompensationSerializesWithBoundary` (boundary admitted\n104|  after the abort with the binding still current).\n105|- Narrowing plants: `compensate-marker-skip` (admits markers differing\n106|  only in non-generation pins; killed by\n107|  `TestJointCommitCompensationRefusesTamperedMarker`),\n108|  `compensate-restore-verify-skip` (admits restores leaving the\n109|  replacement; killed by\n110|  `TestJointCommitCompensationVerifiesRestore/noop_restore`),\n111|  `compensate-restore-ignore` (ignores a failed restore; killed by\n112|  `TestJointCommitCompensationFailsAfterDurableRestore`),\n113|  `compensate-source-swap` / `compensate-rollback-source-swap`\n114|  (restore the wrong bytes; killed by the `*CompensatesBumpFailure`\n115|  entry tests). Preserve-token order swap\n116|  `compensate-verify-before-restore` keeps every call and reorders\n117|  verify-before-restore: the static gate still passes and only the\n118|  behavioral suite fails (killed by\n119|  `TestJointCommitCompensatesBumpFailure` among others).\n120|\n121|### 4. Trust bump — `transactLocked` via `commitDocument`\n122|\n123|- Production call site: `transactLocked`\n124|  (`internal/hosttrust/transact.go`) encodes generation+1 and calls\n125|  `commitDocument` (stage, fsync, 0600, ACL install, atomic rename,\n126|  directory fsync).\n127|- Required lock state: exclusive. Direct callers: `transact` (after\n128|  `convergeLocked`), `JointCommit` (bump step),\n129|  `recoverLocked`/`convergeLocked` (forward completion).\n130|- Intent revalidation: generation ceiling (`MaxGeneration`), no caller\n131|  generation change (`next.Generation == committed.Generation`), plus\n132|  the caller-specific entry rules below.\n133|- Positive tests: joint happy path, lifecycle tests, recovery tests.\n134|- Interleaving negatives: `TestSharedSnapshotSerializesWithExclusive`,\n135|  `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation` (+ separate-store\n136|  twin), `TestLoadCoherentSerializesWithJointCommit`.\n137|- Narrowing plants: `exhaustion` (admits the ceiling generation;\n138|  killed by `TestGenerationExhaustionRefusesMutation`),\n139|  `recover-forward-no-bump` (completes forward without the bump;\n140|  killed by `TestReadSnapshotConvergesInterruptedApply`).\n141|\n142|### 5. Marker stage and removal — `commitDocument` / `removeMarkerLocked`\n143|\n144|- Production call sites: `JointCommit` stages the marker after the\n145|  backstop and removes it on replace failure and after the durable\n146|  bump; `recoverLocked` removes it on forward completion and abort;\n147|  `compensateLocked` removes it on clean abort and re-stages it in the\n148|  sabotage remainder (absent marker plus diverged configuration: the\n149|  in-memory intent still pins the decision, and the re-staged marker\n150|  lets restart recovery resolve the pair instead of admitting it).\n151|- Required lock state: exclusive in all three functions.\n152|- Intent revalidation: closed marker encode/decode (schema, operation,\n153|  absolute config path, 64-hex pins, pins differ, uint53 generation);\n154|  `JointCommit` refuses when a marker is already present after\n155|  leftover convergence (`ErrJointIntervened`).\n156|- Positive tests: `TestJointCommitHappyPath`,\n157|  `TestRecoverCompletesForwardAfterCrash`,\n158|  `TestRecoverAbortsWhenReplacementAbsent`.\n159|- Interleaving negatives: `TestJointCommitConvergesLeftoverThenRefusesStale`,\n160|  `TestJointCommitConvergesAbortedLeftoverThenCommits`,\n161|  `TestJointCommitRefusesIntervenedLeftover`.\n162|- Narrowing plants: `joint-marker-stale` (admits older pinned\n163|  generations; killed by `TestJointCommitRefusesStaleMarkerGeneration`),\n164|  `joint-converge-skip` (call-site removal paired with\n165|  `recover-forward-no-bump`; killed by\n166|  `TestJointCommitConvergesAbortedLeftoverThenCommits`),\n167|  `marker-unreadable` (treats an unreadable marker as absent; killed by\n168|  `TestReadSnapshotRefusesUnreadableMarker`).\n169|\n170|### 6. Recovery and converged reads — `Recover` / `convergeLocked`\n171|\n172|- Production call sites: `Store.Recover` (also automatic in `Open`),\n173|  `convergeLocked` from every exclusive entry point\n174|  (`JointCommit`, `transact`, `Initialize`,\n175|  `WithMutationAuthorization`, `AuthorizeDispatch`) and from\n176|  `lockForConvergedRead` (release-shared/acquire-exclusive upgrade\n177|  when a marker is present, then converge under the exclusive hold).\n178|- Required lock state: exclusive for convergence; the shared fast path\n179|  applies only when no marker is present.\n180|- Intent revalidation: configuration hash selects forward completion\n181|  (replacement hash; source generation bumps, already-bumped only\n182|  removes the marker, anything else refuses), abort (source hash) or\n183|  refusal with the marker kept (anything else, or unreadable state).\n184|- Positive tests: `TestRecoverCompletesForwardAfterCrash`,\n185|  `TestOpenConvergesInterruptedCommit`,\n186|  `TestRecoverConvergesAlreadyBumped`.\n187|- Interleaving negatives: `TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply`\n188|  / `...Rollback` (real child exit 77 at the rename seam),\n189|  `TestSurvivingReaderRefusesDivergedConfig`,\n190|  `TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`,\n191|  `TestReadSnapshotConvergesInterruptedApply` /\n192|  `TestTransactionConvergesPendingMarker` /\n193|  `TestMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleAfterConvergence` (barrier\n194|  matrix), `TestReadSnapshotRefusesIntervention`.\n195|- Narrowing plants: `recover-diverged` (completes forward under a\n196|  diverged generation; killed by\n197|  `TestRecoverRefusesDivergedGeneration`), `dance-converge-ignore` /\n198|  `transact-converge-ignore` / `initialize-converge-ignore` /\n199|  `authorize-converge-ignore` (each admits refused recovery into one\n200|  entry class; killed by the matching `*RefusesIntervention` test).\n201|\n202|### 7. Store setup — `Initialize`\n203|\n204|- Production call site: `Store.Initialize` converges leftover intent,\n205|  refuses when `trust.json` exists, encodes generation 1 and calls\n206|  `commitDocument`.\n207|- Required lock state: exclusive.\n208|- Intent revalidation: leftover convergence first (setup never builds\n209|  beside an unresolved marker); existing trust refuses (setup never\n210|  overwrites committed authority).\n211|- Positive test: `TestOpenCreatesOwnerOnlyLayout` and lifecycle setup.\n212|- Interleaving negative: `TestInitializeRefusesIntervention`.\n213|- Narrowing plant: `initialize-converge-ignore` (admits refused\n214|  recovery into setup; killed by\n215|  `TestInitializeRefusesIntervention`).\n216|\n217|### 8. Enrollment, rotation, revocation, retirement — `transact`\n218|\n219|- Production call sites: `Store.Enroll`, `Store.Rotate`,\n220|  `Store.MarkRetiring`, `Store.Revoke` (and the admitting half of\n221|  `Store.Issue`) mutate through `store.transact`, which converges\n222|  leftover intent and commits via `transactLocked` under the exclusive\n223|  hold.\n224|- Required lock state: exclusive.\n225|- Intent revalidation: per-entry rules — authorized-tuple reproduction\n226|  and profile checks (`Enroll`), single-active-predecessor plus\n227|  24h/leaf-expiry bounds (`Rotate`, `MarkRetiring`), existing\n228|  non-revoked entry (`Revoke`), cross-entry uniqueness over live and\n229|  tombstone entries (`admitEntry`, `checkMappingUnique`), digest\n230|  reproduction (`decodeEntry`).\n231|- Positive tests: `TestEnrollBoundsPerHost`, `TestRotateBoundedWindow`,\n232|  `TestRevokeTombstone`, `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry`, issue\n233|  profile tests.\n234|- Interleaving negatives: same/separate-store revocation contention\n235|  tests (CR3 repairs, still green), stale-mutation refusal\n236|  (`TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration`).\n237|- Narrowing plants: `per-host-bound`, `rotation-expiry`,\n238|  `revoke-state`, `retire-bound`, `retire-expiry`,\n239|  `stale-mutation-refresh`, `expiry-grace`, `digest-root-swap`,\n240|  `unique-root-pair`, `custody-binding` (each killed by its named\n241|  lifecycle/profile test).\n242|\n243|### 9. Credential files — `writeCustodyFile` and uncommitted cleanup\n244|\n245|- Production call sites: `Store.Issue` and `Store.Rotate` create the\n246|  credential directory (`ensureOwnerDir`), install\n247|  `certificate.pem`/`private-key.pem`/`root.pem` via\n248|  `writeCustodyFile` (0600 staging, ACL install before key material is\n249|  written, fsync, atomic rename, owner verification), then run the\n250|  admitting `transact`. On any failure the deferred cleanup removes\n251|  only that operation's own uncommitted directory.\n252|- Required lock state: none — the exception row. Custody files are\n253|  inert until the admitting trust commit: a crash can only leave\n254|  files without authority, never authority without verifiable\n255|  custody. Directory names are fresh-key digests, so concurrent\n256|  issuers never share a directory, and cleanup only removes the\n257|  directory the failed operation created (no other operation can\n258|  reference its unknown digests).\n259|- Intent revalidation: use-time `ValidateCustody` (owner-only regular\n260|  files, PEM shape, private/public match, profile, host binding,\n261|  contained-leaf-equals-directory-name) before every use\n262|  (`revalidateApplyV4`, dispatch authorization).\n263|- Positive tests: `TestIssueSelfEnrollsActive`, rotation happy paths.\n264|- Interleaving negative: not applicable as a pair race (unique inert\n265|  directories); misuse is refused at use time\n266|  (`TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`, `TestCustodyRefusals`).\n267|- Narrowing plants: `custody-0644` (admits world-readable files;\n268|  killed by `TestCustodyRefusals/world_readable_trust_file`),\n269|  `custody-binding` (admits root-digest directory names; killed by\n270|  `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`).\n271|\n272|### 10. Legacy v1/v2/v3 migration — `replaceDurably` in `migrate`\n273|\n274|- Production call site: `migrate`\n275|  (`internal/config/migration.go`) calls `replaceDurably` directly.\n276|  This path predates the joint barrier and holds no authorization\n277|  lock.\n278|- Required lock state: none — the legacy row. It stays fail-closed\n279|  against joint intent in both directions: a joint commit's in-lock\n280|  revalidation refuses a source the legacy path changed\n281|  (`ErrMigrationV4StaleSource`), and a legacy replacement beside an\n282|  outstanding marker diverges from the pins, so every converged\n283|  reader refuses `ErrJointIntervened` instead of admitting the mix.\n284|- Intent revalidation: `Load` validation of the selected source\n285|  before anything durable is written; backup publication before the\n286|  replacement; refusal leaves the directory exactly as found.\n287|- Positive tests: `TestMigrateProductionEntryCreatesOwnerOnlyBackupAndCompleteVersion2`,\n288|  `TestMigrateProductionEntryMapsLegacyTerminalToVersion3AndIsIdempotent`.\n289|- Interleaving negative:\n290|  `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence` (legacy v1-to-v2\n291|  replacement beside a staged marker; `LoadCoherent` and a fresh\n292|  `Open` refuse with the marker kept).\n293|- Narrowing plant: `v4-explicit-label` is label precision (marked as\n294|  such); the semantic legacy gates predate this census and keep\n295|  their existing refusal tests.\n296|\n297|### 11. Backups and staging files\n298|\n299|- Production call sites: backups (`.bak.<version>`,\n300|  `.pre-rollback.<version>`) publish inside `replaceDurably` under\n301|  the same hold as rows 1/2/10 (0600 staging, hard-link publication,\n302|  existing-name byte comparison). Config staging\n303|  (`.ax-config-*`, `.ax-config-restore-*`) and trust staging\n304|  (`.trust-stage-*`, `.custody-stage-*`, `lock-stage-*`) are created\n305|  and renamed only inside the row-1..9 helpers; readers never select\n306|  them and failures remove them.\n307|- Required lock state: as the owning row; leftover staging from a\n308|  crash is inert by name.\n309|- Intent revalidation: backup bytes must equal the pre-migration\n310|  source exactly; classification pinned by\n311|  `TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy` (byte-exact config copy,\n312|  no key material, 0600, exclusion match, no credential files under\n313|  the config dir).\n314|- Positive tests: backup assertions in the apply/rollback happy\n315|  paths, `TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded`.\n316|- Interleaving negative: a backup published by a failed replace\n317|  (replace fails after backup publication) is inert and excluded;\n318|  the next attempt reuses it only on byte equality.\n319|- Narrowing plant: covered through the owning rows; backup-name\n320|  matching is pinned by `TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded` and\n321|  the exclusion matcher tests.\n322|\n323|### 12. Lock file creation — `CreateExclusive` in `openLock`\n324|\n325|- Production call site: `openLock` (unix and windows) creates the\n326|  lock file atomically (`O_CREAT|O_EXCL` / `CREATE_NEW`); a loser of\n327|  the creation race opens the existing inode/file instead of\n328|  replacing a live lock.\n329|- Required lock state: none — creation is the atomic primitive, not\n330|  a pair mutation. No production path renames over the lock file.\n331|- Intent revalidation: `verifyLockFile` (owner-only custody;\n332|  non-regular files refuse immediately; other failures retry within\n333|  the 500ms creation-to-secure window).\n334|- Positive tests: `TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock`\n335|  (returnedWhileHeld=false, sameInode=true),\n336|  `TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock`.\n337|- Interleaving negative: `TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock` is itself\n338|  the deterministic barrier port (child paused after the absence\n339|  observation ends on the same inode and waits out the held lock);\n340|  `TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock` covers 8-way same-inode\n341|  attach plus open-blocks-on-held-exclusive.\n342|- Narrowing plant: `lock-replacing-init` (publishes the lock with a\n343|  replacing rename; killed with genuine\n344|  `returnedWhileHeld=true sameInode=false` by\n345|  `TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock`).\n346|- STATED BOUND: `verifyLockFile` rechecks current path custody but\n347|  does not pin an inode: an owner replacing the lock file externally\n348|  between retries can pass a later retry. No production initializer\n349|  replaces the inode; no protection against external owner\n350|  replacement is claimed.\n351|\n352|## Cross-row notes\n353|\n354|- Spurious-bump corner: a bump whose rename landed but whose commit\n355|  still reported failure aborts to (source, source+1) rather than\n356|  completing forward. Forward completion would risk power-loss\n357|  incoherence (unproven rename durability with the marker gone);\n358|  the abort direction only invalidates stale bindings, which refuse\n359|  safely. No test can distinguish this corner from a failed bump,\n360|  and none claims to.\n361|- Power loss beyond fsync is a stated bound everywhere: process\n362|  crashes are covered by stage+fsync+rename+dirsync with real\n363|  child-process tests; disk honesty under power loss is not\n364|  established here.\n365|- Windows runtime execution is unverified (no runner): the DACL\n366|  implementation plus 7 native build-tagged tests are present with\n367|  cross-build/vet evidence only. Config-dir backup DACLs inherit\n368|  user-profile ACLs as a stated bound. Row 15 of the AC matrix\n369|  counts as implementation present, NOT driven.\n370|- The static gate scans non-test sources only: test files stage\n371|  fixtures through direct writes by design. Production can never\n372|  call test helpers (Go excludes `_test.go` from normal builds).\n373|  Direct `ReadFile`/`Lstat`/`Stat` calls are reads, not pair\n374|  mutations, and are intentionally outside the gate; `Chmod`/\n375|  `MkdirAll` are custody setup covered by the custody tests.\n376|- Diagnostic bundle export remains UNOWNED (no board task); the\n377|  row-21 matcher handoff persists on the seven owning tasks.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c547","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aba9-d1ff-7602-bf9f-32a3aa09bb6c"},"sequence":254,"recorded_at":1780531400000503,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e6495f39-5100-411c-852e-b85f9d8475b0"},"call_id":"call_01a0abaa67c070f69d0336db3d345783","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-2ez769 rework results rev6 — CR5 finding repaired as a class\n2|\n3|Producer rework after CR5 changes-requested verdict (RUN-260916-f8925e,\n4|Astra low). Managed base `a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903`\n5|(v0.6.0 adoption trunk in place; no base move needed). Worktree left\n6|UNCOMMITTED on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6` for handoff\n7|snapshot; no producer commit, no main push. Producer: Muse\n8|(muse-spark), 2026-09-16. This brief governs; superseded briefs are\n9|scope context only.\n10|\n11|RED-first: the exact CR5 probe `TestReviewerRestoreCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit`\n12|was copied onto pre-fix source and reproduced FAIL (exit 1,\n13|`unlocked recovery replaced admitted Config4 with 3.0.0 without a\n14|generation change: before=4 after=4`, log in evidence tarball). The 7\n15|original reviewer probes passed pre-fix (baseline log) and re-pass on\n16|the final source (final log).\n17|\n18|## Preservation (re-verified this run)\n19|\n20|- Worktree implementation bytes verified identical to CR5 candidate\n21|  tree `a823eb20` on all 53 patch paths (scratch\n22|  `git archive a89328c` + rev5 patch application + per-path `cmp`)\n23|  before any edit.\n24|- 4 tracked RPC paths CLEAN vs HEAD; no `UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md` or\n25|  `internal/rpcwire` remnants; none of those paths in the candidate\n26|  diff.\n27|- Control-root backup\n28|  `.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910`:\n29|  15/15 files match manifest SHA256 (recomputed).\n30|- Parked delta `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/parked-rpc-delta-260910`:\n31|  11/11 untracked files match the control manifest SHA256.\n32|- Checkpointed SSH/peer bytes untouched: rev6 touches only\n33|  `internal/hosttrust/{joint,errors}.go`,\n34|  `internal/config/{migration_v4_apply,migration_v4_helpers}.go`,\n35|  test files, the two mutation harnesses, and `LOGBOOK.md` (manifest\n36|  diff vs rev5 names exactly these files plus the 2 new test files).\n37|  Zero `sshtransport` changes; `peeridentity` delta still only\n38|  `v4_interop_test.go`.\n39|\n40|## CR5 F1 resolution (production mechanism, not assertions)\n41|\n42|`JointCommit` now takes the restore closure and compensates a failed\n43|generation bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked` in\n44|`internal/hosttrust/joint.go`): the marker is re-read\n45|(custody-verified, closed decode) and compared pin-for-pin with the\n46|staged intent; the configuration hash must equal the replacement pin\n47|(source-present skips the restore; anything else refuses with the\n48|marker kept); the restore runs; the restored bytes are re-read and\n49|must equal the source pin before the marker aborts. Committed trust\n50|is deliberately never re-read for the decision (the fault that broke\n51|the bump must not break the abort; an apparently durable bump is\n52|unproven exactly because its commit reported failure). The unlocked\n53|`restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted; `ErrJointReplacementDurable`\n54|now reports the clean abort (original bump refusal preserved) and the\n55|new `ErrJointCompensationFailed` reports compensation that cannot\n56|complete (restore failed, pins moved, marker unreadable), with the\n57|marker kept for operator resolution and the replacement left for\n58|forward recovery. `applyV4`/`rollbackV4` map compensation failure to\n59|the existing `ErrMigrationSync`/`ErrMigrationRecovery` compound;\n60|signatures of the production entries are unchanged.\n61|\n62|Post-fix, the original probe shape cannot fail behaviorally: its\n63|in-seam convergence attempt blocks in `flock LOCK_SH` on the held\n64|exclusive lock (45s-timeout goroutine dump in evidence shows\n65|`compensateLocked` → restore closure → `writeTempReplace` → seam →\n66|`LoadCoherent` → `lockForConvergedRead` → `Flock`). The port\n67|`TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` keeps the\n68|reviewer's final-state assertion with the race staged as a goroutine\n69|against the gated restore.\n70|\n71|## Write-path census + gate\n72|\n73|`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` (attached outcome)\n74|enumerates all 12 write paths over `config.toml`, backups,\n75|`trust.json`, the marker, the lock file and credential files, each\n76|with production call site, required lock state, intent revalidation,\n77|positive test, interleaving negative and narrowing plant. Notable\n78|rows: legacy `migrate` (no lock, fail-closed, pinned by the new\n79|`TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), credential files\n80|(no lock, inert-until-admitted with unique fresh-key directories),\n81|lock creation (atomic `O_CREAT|O_EXCL`/`CREATE_NEW`, no lock held),\n82|and the sabotage remainder (vanished marker + diverged config\n83|re-stages the marker so restart recovery resolves instead of\n84|admitting).\n85|\n86|`TestWritePathCensusGate` (committed,\n87|`internal/config/writepath_census_test.go`) statically fails any\n88|pair mutation outside the censused rows (JointCommit-closure rule\n89|for the config helpers, lock-held allowlists for trust/marker\n90|helpers, custody-site allowlists, raw-rename/remove/create\n91|allowlists); zero violations on this source.\n92|`TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller` is the control plant (3\n93|rogue shapes flagged, censused shapes pass).\n94|\n95|## AC coverage: 19 of 21 rows driven through production entry points\n96|\n97|| # | Row | Production call / named test | Result |\n98||---|---|---|---|\n99|| 1 | Closed Config4 | config.Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals | pass |\n100|| 2 | Historical compat + explicit migration | config.Migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade | pass |\n101|| 3 | Closed trust document | hosttrust.DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals | pass |\n102|| 4 | Missing/corrupt/unreadable trust | hosttrust ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty, TestReadSnapshotRefusesUnreadableMarker | pass |\n103|| 5 | Fresh issuance | hosttrust IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile | pass |\n104|| 6 | Exact profile + time bounds | hosttrust VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry | pass |\n105|| 7 | Explicit tuple enrollment | hosttrust Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals | pass; OOB human verification remains operator act |\n106|| 8 | Mapping uniqueness | hosttrust DecodeTrust+admitEntry / duplicate-root/key/digest rows | pass |\n107|| 9 | Rotation/retirement bounds | hosttrust Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry | pass |\n108|| 10 | Revocation tombstones | hosttrust Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls | pass |\n109|| 11 | Old-generation mutation refusal | hosttrust WithMutationAuthorization / TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration, TestMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleAfterConvergence | pass |\n110|| 12 | Shared authorization serialization | hosttrust Open/openLock, WithMutationAuthorization+Revoke / TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock, TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock, TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation, TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithSeparateStoreRevocation | pass |\n111|| 13 | Coherent config+trust snapshot | config LoadCoherent / TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply, TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedRollback, TestSurvivingReaderRefusesDivergedConfig, TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit, TestRollbackV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit | pass (was CR5 FAIL) |\n112|| 14 | Unix owner custody | hosttrust Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory | pass on darwin |\n113|| 15 | Windows equivalent ACLs | hosttrust verifyOwner/installOwnerOnlyACL/secureStaged / custody_windows_test.go (7 native tests) | NOT DRIVEN: code + tests present, vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified (no runner) |\n114|| 16 | Complete peers + selected credential | config PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates | pass |\n115|| 17 | Exact preview + confirmation | config ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops | pass |\n116|| 18 | Current source/generation apply | config applyV4+JointCommit / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration, revalidate* tests | pass, incl. in-lock revalidation |\n117|| 19 | Crash-durable config/trust pair | config applyV4/rollbackV4 + hosttrust JointCommit/compensateLocked/Recover/converge / TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration (fixed), surviving-reader crash tests, barrier matrix, 6 compensation race tests, 2 entry clean-abort tests | pass (was CR5 FAIL unlocked error recovery) |\n118|| 20 | Explicit backup rollback | config RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4*, TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded, TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy | pass |\n119|| 21 | Secret exclusion across export surfaces | hosttrust MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / matcher tests + persisted handoff + 7 owner notes; diagnostics unowned | NOT DRIVEN: matcher enforced, no consumer calls it yet |\n120|\n121|Stated bounds (not production-driven here): rows 15 and 21 as above,\n122|retained exactly as CR5 accounted them; live TLS 1.3\n123|launch/handshake/hello/dispatch and stream close-down belong to the\n124|RPC transport task; peer-side distribution of enrollment/rotation/\n125|revocation is operator duty per spec; power-loss durability beyond\n126|fsync; config-dir backup DACLs on Windows (profile ACLs +\n127|exclusion); `verifyLockFile` 500ms retry rechecks custody without\n128|pinning an inode (no claim against external owner replacement of\n129|lock files); the spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\n130|\n131|## Negative + mutation evidence (rerun this run, exact final source)\n132|\n133|- hosttrust battery `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-hosttrust-rev6/`:\n134|  29 narrowing mutants KILLED by named tests (incl. new\n135|  compensate-marker-skip, compensate-restore-verify-skip,\n136|  compensate-restore-ignore, compensate-verify-before-restore) + 1\n137|  call-site mutant joint-converge-skip KILLED (paired with\n138|  recover-forward-no-bump, as in rev5) + 1 neutral SURVIVED control\n139|  (exit 0). Harness exit 0. results.json + table.md + manifest.json\n140|  (31 source digests, head a89328c).\n141|- config battery `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-config-rev6/`:\n142|  6 semantic narrowing KILLED (incl. new compensate-source-swap,\n143|  compensate-rollback-source-swap) + 1 label-precision KILLED\n144|  (marked LABEL-PRECISION) + 1 neutral passed. Harness exit 0.\n145|  results.json + table.md + manifest.json (34 source digests, head\n146|  a89328c).\n147|- Every reported exit comes from the real command status\n148|  (subprocess returncode; no pipelines). All 39 plants pre-verified\n149|  to match exactly once; no compile-failure, unapplied or\n150|  empty-selection kills. Mutant sources, overlay.json, standalone\n151|  test.logs and final counts preserved per probe.\n152|- `compensate-verify-before-restore` is the preserve-token\n153|  behavioral mutant for the static gate: it reorders\n154|  verify-before-restore while keeping every call, so the call-site\n155|  gate still passes and only the behavioral suite fails (killed by\n156|  `TestJointCommitCompensatesBumpFailure` among others; the\n157|  harnesses run the full behavioral suites). No other gate searches\n158|  source text for a token (all gates operate on decoded\n159|  values/DER/parsed TOML/file bytes/ACEs).\n160|- In-test finding: the new boundary race tests initially deadlocked\n161|  by reading trust on the main goroutine after the replacement seam\n162|  (lock held by the faulted op); the request now binds pre-seam with\n163|  an in-code comment. Final runs are deadlock-free, including under\n164|  `-race`.\n165|\n166|## Gates rerun this run (all exit 0)\n167|\n168|gofmt clean (413 files scanned); `go vet ./...`;\n169|`GOOS=windows go vet ./...`; `go build ./...`\n170|darwin+linux+windows; `go test ./... -count=1` (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1\n171|pre-existing env-gated SKIP TestDumpSweepSites); `-cover`\n172|hosttrust 77.9% config 93.3% peeridentity 97.5% secprim 94.4%;\n173|`-race ./...` 26 ok with no `DATA RACE`; tracecheck ok\n174|(contracts=63 sections=36 cases=101); catalog freshness pin +\n175|generate + clean diff (no collateral); cigate contracts 6/6 +\n176|claims 6/6 + target derivation 2/2; fuzz smoke 13/13 with `fuzz:\n177|elapsed` each; fixtures secprim 51 pass + secconftest 59 pass with\n178|0 skips; `git diff --check` clean. `task-board validate` exits 0\n179|with 201 board-wide issues, 0 referencing this task (exit 0\n180|alongside listed issues is not proof of a clean board). 7 original\n181|reviewer probes re-pass on the final source. No hosted CI used;\n182|all gates executed locally.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
